WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.350
Well, let's get crackin'.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.580
Let's-a-go.

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.920
Stop messing around and start!

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:34.210
Since fall is for reading...

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:36.920
...I've been doing a lot of reading.

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:38.720
That's unusual.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.800
Even though it's for an educational purpose...

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.720
...the expenses are piling up.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:43.850
You don't have to buy them.

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:46.060
Couldn't you just go to a library or something?

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:47.720
They actually have some stuff you'd want.

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:48.600
Nah.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.490
A library wouldn't have manga.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:54.020
<i>Reading, huh...</i>

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.270
<i>They mean books, you know...</i>

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.150
Can't concentrate...

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.830
Well, you have to take a break every now and then.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.080
Like this.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:17.130
I'll do a little gaming to relax.

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:21.630
It's Ms. Kuroi.

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:22.840
Hey!

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:25.180
Stop playin' and get to studyin'!

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:28.220
I'll be mighty pissed if your grades are bad.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:29.390
<i>Phooey!</i>

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:31.100
<i>The authorities can even find me here!</i>

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:33.390
<i>Don't do this to me, Teacher!</i>

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:36.860
This game suddenly isn't as fun
with all these interruptions.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:43.070
How did you study for tests when you were a student?

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:46.700
Played or slept when I couldn't concentrate.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:48.740
Nothing really special.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:50.620
That's the same as me.

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:53.580
But as an authority figure, I have to be strict.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.080
<i>I get what she means...</i>

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.790
<i>...but it still feels unfair!</i>

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:03.930
This time, I plan on setting
goals and studying bit by bit.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.590
Sis, teach me the stuff I don't get.

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:08.430
Then let's study together.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:15.440
So in this case, <i>x</i> would equal...

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:16.810
What is it?

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:19.980
I just realized that my TV show's about to start.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:21.360
In today's episode...

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.320
...a weekly magazine reporter...

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:26.280
...spreads word of the main character's pregnancy.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.700
So you're going to watch TV?

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:29.950
It's okay.

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:31.240
I'm taping it.

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.120
Um...

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:50.140
I get sleepy whenever there's
a bunch of questions I don't get...

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:51.890
Which means you're always sleepy?

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.690
I probably shouldn't overextend
myself right off the bat...

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:57.810
...so I'll call it a day.

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:58.520
Okay.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:01.400
I see you're already losing your willpower.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:05.380
I still can't concentrate!

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:06.400
Okay.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.450
You want a trick for studying for a test?

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:12.410
I was wondering how you study.

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:13.870
Let's see...

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:17.540
If you concentrate too hard, you'll wear yourself out.

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:21.170
In my case, I just follow my usual habits.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:24.380
So I'm pretty confident about today's test.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:26.220
I feel so enlightened.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:29.140
Aren't your usual habits a little risky?

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:30.680
You don't do anything.

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:33.850
But it's so cute...

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:36.350
And its claws are venomous.

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:37.190
My...

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:39.940
So it's actually quite frightening.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.060
Yo.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:42.230
Kagami.

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:43.270
How'd it go?

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:45.360
This one was pretty bad.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:47.570
Though I maintained my standing.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:49.570
So you also do bad sometimes.

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:52.780
Because Sis helped me out.

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:55.790
As a result, I did better than usual.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:57.290
How about you?

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:00.460
Strangely enough, I did bad.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:01.580
And I was so sure I'd do well.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:03.170
Nothing strange about it at all.

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:04.670
It was inevitable.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:06.010
But you know...

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:09.220
...I was feeling that birds of a feather flock together.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:10.550
For example...

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:14.260
Kagami and Miyuki-san are both class representatives.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:17.120
Kagami and I both like games.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.270
Well, different genres though.

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:21.190
You play dating sims and RPGs.

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:22.730
And I play shooters.

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:26.360
I was thinking that Tsukasa and I were both stupid...

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:28.330
...but there was a significant gap this time.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:32.110
Well, I'm not really concerned about doing bad.

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:33.410
Be a little concerned.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:36.160
If you slack off because everybody else also did bad...

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:37.660
...you'll fall behind.

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:40.920
Actually...

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:44.130
I didn't make any bets with my dad...

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:46.000
...so I'm not really angry.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.760
You're gonna grow up to be a bad person.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:50.510
If you're gonna copy Miyuki...

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:52.130
...take notes regularly...

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:53.930
...instead of waiting till tests are coming up.

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:56.310
Miyuki-san is really methodical.

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:58.430
Textbook example of a type A person.

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:00.980
Many people have told me that...

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:03.230
...but I'm actually type O.

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:04.730
You're type O?

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:06.150
Never would have guessed.

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:07.280
However...

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:11.740
According to this book...

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:14.820
...I possess many of the qualities...

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:16.740
...characteristic of type O people.

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:18.490
For example...

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:20.790
It's said that type O people tend to be...

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:22.460
...childish and innocent...

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:24.040
...which describes me perfectly.

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:28.090
Type O people tend to be pushy and possessive...

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:31.220
I guess there's another side to Miyuki-san.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:32.970
You're probably type A.

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:36.550
But a lot of people mistake me for a type B.

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:39.520
Type A people are skilled in
social functions and considerate.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:42.020
They tend to seek peaceful human interaction?

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:43.520
Does this even match you?

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:46.150
I can be really sensitive to the situation.

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:48.270
Only when it's something you're interested in.

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:50.110
I'm gentle and attentive to other people.

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:51.820
When it involves homework.

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:56.070
What about you, Kagami?

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:56.660
Me?

00:06:56.990 --> 00:06:58.160
I'm type B.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:03.580
So you're laid-back, rude, erratic,
unconventional, naive, and insolent, huh?

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:04.670
What about it?

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:06.830
Then Tsukasa's type AB?

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:07.790
What's that supposed to mean?

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:08.500
Why?

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:09.670
Just a hunch.

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:11.630
If you go by personality...

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:12.840
...Tsukasa would be type A...

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:15.180
...and Kagami would be type B.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:17.470
We're both type B.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.100
And like, we're twins.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.010
That's right.

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:21.100
Brain fart.

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:23.180
And I'm not as laid-back as you are.

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:24.850
Speaking of horoscopes...

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:27.900
...I've also heard of ones for animals and sushi.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:29.110
Sushi?

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:31.360
Let's see...

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:32.360
Miyuki-san is...

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:34.780
So Miyuki would be salmon roe.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:36.360
Still high-class, I see.

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:38.570
I love salmon roe!

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:39.080
And?

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:40.470
What about Tsukasa and me?

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:44.790
Cucumber roll.

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:46.460
A cucumber roll, huh?

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:48.830
Well, I guess it counts as sushi.

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:50.210
This is pretty accurate.

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:51.920
And what about you?

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:53.080
Me?

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:56.090
Sliced ginger?

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:58.760
It says sliced ginger!

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:02.060
Don't look down on ginger!

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:02.770
Well...

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:05.140
You can't have sushi without it...

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:08.440
...and the horoscope's description is positive.

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:09.980
That's true.

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:12.530
And cucumber rolls count as sushi, right?

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:15.490
Hello?

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:16.450
Konata?

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:18.360
About the blood type conversation today...

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:19.910
Just to make sure you know...

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:22.990
...fraternal twins can have different blood types...

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:25.290
...so your guess wasn't wrong.

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:27.920
Sounded like you got the wrong impression.

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:30.420
Thanks awfully.

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:31.750
You're an honest person.

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:34.210
I'm starting to see the type A in you.

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:35.210
Oh, yeah...

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:38.300
There was a psychic reading on TV.

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:40.050
With those things...

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:45.220
...you'll guess right with some
people and wrong with some people...

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:49.270
...so you'd at least make one correct guess somewhere.

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:50.440
Kagami...

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:52.900
Don't be so pragmatic...

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:54.940
You'll never have fun in life.

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:57.320
Act more like your age.

00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:58.530
<i>Tsukasa.</i>

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:00.030
<i>You worked hard this time.</i>

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:05.370
<i>Kagami did worse than usual.</i>

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:09.460
<i>But she still got a higher score, huh...</i>

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:13.440
Good work, girls.

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:15.420
How should I put it...

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:17.380
You did the best you could...

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:18.010
Ooh.

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:19.430
Tsukasa worked hard.

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:22.390
But Kagami still scored higher.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:23.600
Hey, Matsuri.

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:25.470
Can't you be more considerate?

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:29.640
Good morning!

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:31.480
Oh, good morning.

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:35.520
I envy how the two of you are such fine young ladies.

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:35.980
Not at all.

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:36.980
You're too kind.

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:40.910
To get such wonderful grades at that Ryouou High...

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:43.120
I wish my children had a fraction of your ability.

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:44.120
<i>It's like...</i>

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:44.530
<i>I'm being praised because I'm her sister...</i>

00:09:44.530 --> 00:09:45.160
Nah.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:46.830
We aren't that impressive.

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:49.000
<i>...so I can't really appreciate it.</i>

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:55.100
Tests are over.

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:57.050
Why don't we go all-out and have some fun?

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:58.510
Sounds good.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:00.840
How about watching a movie for once?

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:02.990
What's in theaters right now?

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:04.900
There's a great one right now.

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:05.720
What is it?

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:07.180
You could call it a splatter film...

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:11.210
...but it still has some psycho-
suspenseful, shocking horror elements.

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:13.750
Then let's do that!

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:15.770
How about we go home first and meet up later?

00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:17.940
Let's do that! Let's do that!

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:20.210
<i>This isn't fun...</i>

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:22.570
<i>I can't have fun like this!</i>

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:27.120
Still got time. What should we do?

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:29.200
Konata sure is late.

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:30.580
Is she late again?

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:31.750
Maybe...

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:35.540
She couldn't have come before us, right?

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:37.000
Honestly...

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:39.040
The movie's about to start.

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:42.840
When did she...

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:45.300
I couldn't recognize you without that thing...

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:49.060
Anyway, we're short on time so let's go.

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:50.140
Oh, yeah.

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:53.020
Pretend I'm your sister.

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:54.270
Why?

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:55.230
Well...

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:58.110
Then I can buy a child's ticket without looking weird.

00:10:58.110 --> 00:10:59.230
<i>Stupid kid.</i>

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:01.150
<i>She whines about her height all the time...</i>

00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:03.150
<i>...but then she exploits it when she can!</i>

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:04.700
That was terrifying, Take-rin!

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:06.160
You're so adorable.

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:07.700
I'm a little hungry now.

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:08.530
Me too.

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:11.490
And Tsukasa's probably hungry
after screaming so much.

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:13.960
What should we have?

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:15.750
How about a cake buffet?

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:16.920
Sounds great!

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:18.500
The buffet...

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:21.390
A haven for satiating a woman's desires!

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:25.010
They've got so many cakes and drinks.

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:26.050
Sure do.

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:28.510
I wonder if we'll get through every one.

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:30.540
Piece of cake for Kagami.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:34.270
This store has a time limit of one hour.

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:36.810
You can find beverages in the drink corner over there.

00:11:36.810 --> 00:11:39.610
The cakes are located in the showcase over there.

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:41.280
Please help yourself.

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:41.980
Okay!

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:42.790
Bow.

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:47.660
And if you leave an excessive amount of leftovers...

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:51.450
...you'll have to pay an extra fee.

00:11:51.450 --> 00:11:53.920
Please keep that in mind.

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:56.800
Then please enjoy yourselves.

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:00.460
What would be considered an excessive amount?

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:03.510
Some people take a bunch and don't finish.

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:04.010
Come on.

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:04.840
Let's go.

00:12:06.130 --> 00:12:07.300
That's a lot...

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:08.760
Can you finish all that?

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:10.430
What about you?

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:14.180
This is normal for cake.

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:15.640
No sweat.

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:17.350
Time to eat!

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:24.150
Delicious!

00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:25.650
<i>And that one!</i>

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:27.150
<i>And this one!</i>

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:36.750
I'm in pain now...

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:39.790
We should have slowed down after the first plate.

00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:41.460
I've got heartburn.

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:42.290
Peek.

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:45.710
But we have to pay extra if we leave leftovers.

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:47.960
That's bad!

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:54.930
It hurts...

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:56.520
I-I can't do it...

00:12:58.480 --> 00:12:59.560
We're almost out of time.

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:04.780
Oh, Kagami!

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:06.490
She's on her second wind!

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:08.110
It'd be a waste otherwise!

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:13.410
Impossible.

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:15.040
No! No!

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:16.950
If you drink too much water...

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:19.000
...you won't be able to eat any more!

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:21.920
Just stuff down what you can...

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:24.670
...and wash it down with water at the very end!

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:26.670
Don't sit there looking impressed

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:28.340
Get to eating!

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:29.720
I can't eat another bite...

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:31.890
You can handle pudding or Bavarian cream!

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:32.930
Here.

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:35.680
Can't you eat it?

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:37.810
I'm stuffed, too!

00:13:37.810 --> 00:13:39.810
I'm out, man...

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:41.690
You can just pour the pudding down your throat!

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:43.900
Hurry it up!

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:45.940
<i>This isn't fun...</i>

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:46.070
<i>I can't have fun like this!</i>

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:48.150
C'mon! Get with it!

00:13:48.150 --> 00:13:48.360
<i>I can't have fun like this!</i>

00:13:48.650 --> 00:13:49.860
Tests are over...

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:52.660
...so I did some hardcore gaming...

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:54.780
...which is why I'm so sleepy...

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:56.950
If you studied that hard...

00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:58.370
...your tests would have gone differently.

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:01.960
Recent dating sims have a bunch of save points...

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:04.500
...but I can never find a good place to stop.

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:06.550
I'm the do-it-in-one-sitting type.

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:08.050
I've been wondering...

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:10.170
A student shouldn't be able to buy those.

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:11.380
How do you buy them?

00:14:12.090 --> 00:14:14.010
I get my dad to buy them for me.

00:14:14.010 --> 00:14:14.550
<i>No way!</i>

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:15.640
<i>I've been thinking...</i>

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:17.770
<i>Your family's pretty crazy...</i>

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:19.520
<i>You actually go buy them, Pops?</i>

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:21.140
<i>And don't ask him, daughter.</i>

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:23.940
So I'm really sleepy.

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:26.730
You probably don't play games, Miyuki-san.

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:29.570
I don't have a game console...

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:31.740
...but I have a computer so
I occasionally play some games.

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:33.820
What do you play?

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:34.870
Didn't expect this!

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:37.410
Games like Solitaire and Minesweeper.

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:39.080
It can get pretty intense.

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:41.290
<i>They're games...</i>

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:43.330
<i>...but you've got it wrong, Miyuki-san.</i>

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:45.130
But I know what you mean.

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:46.960
It's actually easy to get absorbed...

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:49.090
...in those kinds of simple games.

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:51.380
What kind of scores do you get, Yuki-chan?

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:53.470
Luck is a factor in Solitaire...

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:56.100
...but I often score over ten thousand.

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:59.890
As for Minesweeper, I completed expert in
under one hundred seconds the other day.

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:04.650
<i>These kind of people really get into this kind of stuff...</i>

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:10.690
There was a lot of sports stuff this year.

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:15.700
That one athlete got gold in
figure skating at the Winter Olympics.

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:18.280
And there was quite a fuss over high school baseball.

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:20.280
There was that incredibly long match.

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:22.160
And the Handkerchief Prince.

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:23.580
Speaking of baseball...

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:25.750
That one player went to America, right?

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:28.670
Is the Japan Series already over?

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:29.550
A long time ago.

00:15:29.550 --> 00:15:30.210
No way!

00:15:30.210 --> 00:15:31.920
Were there any bargain sales?

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:35.260
This year's Japan Series was
between that team and that team...

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:38.760
...so there weren't any supermarket
or department store chains involved.

00:15:38.760 --> 00:15:41.220
But they had a commemorative sale.

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:46.350
But it was probably just a sale on ham.

00:15:46.350 --> 00:15:48.400
Did they do that...?

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:51.280
Anyway, I need to remember to do a check next year...

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:52.690
Knowing you...

00:15:52.690 --> 00:15:54.650
...you're probably just gonna buy snacks.

00:15:54.650 --> 00:15:55.780
I'm not.

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:58.200
I need stuff like salt, sugar, and soy sauce.

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:00.680
Those kinds of household staples.

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:02.870
Well...

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:06.370
Kagami wouldn't understand
what I'm talking about, right?

00:16:06.370 --> 00:16:07.710
So sorry!

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:09.540
So I suck at household chores!

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:15.380
Eyedrops?

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:16.780
Want me to help?

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:18.760
Thank you so much.

00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:19.430
Okay.

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:21.230
Lie down.

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:22.260
Yes.

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:23.430
Okay...

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:24.930
Relax.

00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:26.440
Y-Yes.

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:27.980
Then here I go.

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:32.360
Okay.

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:33.780
Relax your muscles.

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:34.680
Yes.

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:39.740
Um...

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:40.870
I'm sorry.

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:43.030
I'm not doing this on purpose...

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:44.870
Your face...

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:46.250
...scares me!

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:53.840
With mail-in prize contests...

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:56.970
...the problem is how it takes
forever to receive the item.

00:16:57.220 --> 00:17:02.350
That's why I came up with a way to
have fun twice as you play, Kagamin.

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:03.220
What's that?

00:17:03.220 --> 00:17:05.720
First, you enjoy the game like you're at a festival.

00:17:05.720 --> 00:17:10.270
And by the time you've forgotten, the
item arrives and you can be happy again.

00:17:10.270 --> 00:17:12.060
Two for the price of one.

00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:15.730
<i>The waiting's what I can't stand...</i>

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:18.660
<i>You're infinitely positive about
the stuff you enjoy, huh?</i>

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:25.990
Good lucky!

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:26.870
Yes!

00:17:26.870 --> 00:17:29.960
I hope to have a cheerful Lucky Channel today!

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:33.460
We're already on our ninth episode today!

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:35.590
I'm your navigator, Akira Kogami!

00:17:35.590 --> 00:17:37.460
And here's the person that the producer, Itou-san...

00:17:37.460 --> 00:17:41.470
...is going to say "Hey, Shiraishi. Come here a sec." to...

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:43.200
Really?!

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:44.810
I'm Akira-sama's assistant...

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:46.180
100% charged with energy...

00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:47.430
Minoru Shiraishi.

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:48.850
It's a pleasure.

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:49.520
Okay.

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:51.480
Today's the third character introduction.

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:51.730
Tsukasa Hiiragi's turn!

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:52.730
Prop time!

00:17:52.730 --> 00:17:54.150
Roll...

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:56.480
<i>Are you supposed to be a clumsy, slow turtle?</i>

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:57.320
Tsu-
Thi-

00:17:58.070 --> 00:17:58.860
I'm sorry.

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:00.860
This is finally getting exciting!

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:01.780
Yes!

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:02.820
Time to pull up our loincloths...

00:18:02.820 --> 00:18:04.700
...and do our best!

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:05.620
Right, Akira-sama?

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:06.890
Loincloths?

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:09.960
I'm supposed to be an idol...

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:12.080
...so that stuff's kinda...

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:13.630
You handle it.

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:16.170
That's right...

00:18:16.170 --> 00:18:17.340
Uh...

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:20.590
When you pull a loincloth up
so tight that it gets pinched...

00:18:20.590 --> 00:18:21.550
Hey.

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:23.800
I'd like to warn you out of concern.

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:25.430
C-Concern...?

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:27.260
Once an entertainer gets in the gutter...

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:28.350
...it's over.

00:18:28.350 --> 00:18:29.560
So I'm an entertainer...

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:30.100
Also...

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:32.310
You've been using other people's material a lot lately...

00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:33.650
...so watch yourself.

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:34.400
Yes!

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:35.020
Um...

00:18:35.220 --> 00:18:36.520
What are we doing today?

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:39.110
Introducing Tsukasa Hiiragi-san.

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:41.280
That To Hea-

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:42.820
Mi-Mi-Miracle!

00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:43.530
Kamigishi...

00:18:43.530 --> 00:18:45.160
Minorun-run!

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:46.010
Right?

00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:47.870
You can say that?

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:48.790
What do you think?

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:51.870
She reminds me of one of those old idol characters.

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:54.330
Uh, you think so?

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:58.210
Well, I guess you could say
she gives off some idol vibes...

00:18:58.710 --> 00:19:00.050
Don't make me laugh!

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:03.010
Tsukasa Hiiragi's an idol?

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:04.380
Where did that come from?

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:05.760
Y'know...

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:07.850
You're working with me here.

00:19:07.850 --> 00:19:10.520
Learn what a true idol is about already.

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:11.680
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:14.390
Tsukasa Hiiragi is merely a soothing character...

00:19:14.390 --> 00:19:17.060
...with a loser's face.

00:19:18.230 --> 00:19:20.570
A loser's face, huh...

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:21.440
Anyway...

00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:21.650
...who gives a damn about Tsukasa?

00:19:21.650 --> 00:19:23.280
Not even Pops ever hit me!

00:19:23.570 --> 00:19:27.370
I'll teach you the basics of an idol right now.

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:29.620
First is the method for having pictures taken.

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:31.330
Now look here.

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:34.370
This will be a useful lesson for you.

00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:36.210
So put some back into it.

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:36.630
Yes!

00:19:36.740 --> 00:19:39.930
You know how people suddenly
take pictures when you're in the city?

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:41.380
Come on.

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:42.630
Press the shutter.

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:45.010
Looking like a loser...?
Fawn. Fawn. Fawn.

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:46.890
Yeah.

00:19:46.890 --> 00:19:48.550
Like that.

00:19:48.550 --> 00:19:50.850
Props are also important.

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:53.140
You should always carry them around.

00:19:53.140 --> 00:19:53.770
How?

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:59.270
And you won't want to be caught off
guard when you're walking around...

00:19:59.270 --> 00:20:00.790
...so always be attentive.

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:01.650
And...

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:03.650
...make sure you have sparkling white teeth.

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:04.820
Like a doll!

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:05.700
Intense.

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:06.410
And then...

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:08.870
...make sure your eyes are all wide and goggly...

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:10.910
...and only smile with these muscles.

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:11.660
<i>Jeepers!</i>

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:14.580
And you want a natural expression.

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:17.870
Like if someone suddenly turns a camera on you...

00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:19.950
Akira's, like, whoa!

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:21.570
Like that.

00:20:22.590 --> 00:20:24.050
Natural, you say...

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:26.430
Also, as a variation...

00:20:26.430 --> 00:20:27.510
...if you're going with a guy into a ho—

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:29.090
Oh, no!

00:20:29.090 --> 00:20:31.010
It's time to say goodbye!

00:20:31.010 --> 00:20:39.310
So send us any questions or
comments about the show please!

00:20:39.310 --> 00:20:41.730
You can also send us messages
about the radio show and our home page!

00:20:41.730 --> 00:20:42.190
Okay!

00:20:42.190 --> 00:20:43.530
Then look forward to next week.

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:44.970
Bye-bee!

00:20:46.740 --> 00:20:48.740
We had a photo shoot, right?

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:49.700
Yes, we did.

00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:51.580
How was it?
The one where I was in the cardigan.

00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:53.580
That was cute...

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:54.370
Shankya!

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:57.120
What's wrong?
It was cute?

00:20:57.120 --> 00:20:57.830
Yeah, well...

00:20:57.830 --> 00:20:59.330
Everyone said it looked cute.

00:20:59.330 --> 00:20:59.920
Guess so.

00:20:59.920 --> 00:21:01.210
Yep.
You were on a roll.

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:02.250
Sure was.

00:21:02.250 --> 00:21:03.460
Looked fun.

00:21:03.460 --> 00:21:04.960
The upturned eyes...

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:05.670
...with the uh...

00:21:05.670 --> 00:21:06.970
...arms crossed below my face...

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:07.970
...was really fun!

00:21:08.470 --> 00:21:08.880
Yes.

00:21:08.880 --> 00:21:09.630
Are you hooked now?

00:21:09.630 --> 00:21:11.010
Including the cross-dressing, yes.

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:11.930
I'm hooked.

00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:13.010
Did you check the pictures?

00:21:13.010 --> 00:21:13.930
No, I didn't.

00:21:14.510 --> 00:21:15.560
The manager...

00:21:15.560 --> 00:21:16.060
Yes.

00:21:16.060 --> 00:21:17.140
...checked the pictures...

00:21:17.140 --> 00:21:17.390
Yes.

00:21:17.390 --> 00:21:20.730
...and said there were some
questionable ones to be honest.

00:21:20.730 --> 00:21:22.980
Well, I had a bunch of stiffy shots...

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:24.270
...so those are probably gone.

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:26.530
Sorry! Sorry!

00:21:26.530 --> 00:21:28.280
Made a little oopsie.

00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:29.780
I'll actually sing the next one.

00:21:29.820 --> 00:21:32.200
And she's already ordering another song.

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:33.660
Let me have the remote for once.

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:34.700
Okay.

00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:36.450
Have you guys decided, Tsukasa?

00:21:36.450 --> 00:21:37.750
It'll be a little longer.

00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:40.460
I don't listen to music much
so I don't know many songs.

00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:41.170
That's okay.

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:42.960
I'll sing in the meantime.

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:43.750
Hey.

00:21:43.750 --> 00:21:45.590
Don't just sing anime songs.

00:21:45.590 --> 00:21:47.680
This isn't an anime song.

00:21:53.300 --> 00:21:54.680
I've heard this before.

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:55.510
What is this?

00:21:55.510 --> 00:21:57.020
It's KyonKyon.

00:21:57.020 --> 00:21:59.850
I used to sing this with my dad a lot.

00:21:59.850 --> 00:22:02.310
So you've gone from anime songs to oldies.

00:22:03.020 --> 00:22:06.410
That's an insult to KyonKyon!

00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:13.370
Tsukasa.

00:22:13.370 --> 00:22:15.160
Why don't you just choose a simple song?

00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:16.330
Like a children's song.

00:22:17.120 --> 00:22:19.330
I'm looking through that section, too...

00:22:19.330 --> 00:22:21.250
I'm sorry.

00:22:21.250 --> 00:22:23.120
There's no rush.

00:22:23.120 --> 00:22:25.260
We still have plenty of time.

00:22:56.200 --> 00:22:58.200
Well, next time on Lucky Star:

00:22:58.200 --> 00:22:59.410
I'm Konata.

00:22:59.410 --> 00:23:03.370
In world 3-1 of Super (bleep) Brothers...

00:23:03.370 --> 00:23:05.670
...there's a staircase near the end of the level...

00:23:05.670 --> 00:23:08.590
...where you can jump on the falling turtle...

00:23:08.590 --> 00:23:11.300
If you repeatedly hit the A button...

00:23:11.300 --> 00:23:12.340
...to jump on the turtle...

00:23:12.340 --> 00:23:13.800
...you can get infinite lives...

00:23:13.800 --> 00:23:15.340
...which is great...

00:23:15.340 --> 00:23:16.970
...but if you overdo it...

00:23:16.970 --> 00:23:19.220
...and go over 129 lives...

00:23:19.220 --> 00:23:23.730
...dying once leads to a game over.

00:23:23.730 --> 00:23:26.730
I won't bother going, "So you can't have infinite lives!"

00:23:26.730 --> 00:23:27.560
Maybe it's that.

00:23:27.730 --> 00:23:30.610
A public service announcement from
the folks near Kamitobaguchi Station...

00:23:30.610 --> 00:23:35.740
...that you're supposed to do things in moderation.

00:23:35.740 --> 00:23:36.570
Next time:

00:23:36.570 --> 00:23:37.370
Aspiration.

00:23:37.620 --> 00:23:39.420
Look forward to next time!
